4. Updates
   Licence keys are version-agnostic: a key keeps working with newer builds signed
   by the same vendor public key.  Major upgrades are sold separately unless your
   purchase says otherwise.

5. No warranty / limitation of liability
   The software is provided "as it is", without warranty of any kind.  Key
   recovery involves trying candidates against the blockchain's cryptography; a
   failed or partial search does not entitle you to a refund of anything other than
   what your consumer law requires, and the authors are not liable for lost coins,
   lost time, or decisions taken on the basis of the output.  Always verify a
   recovered key by checking the address it produces before moving funds.

6. Termination
   A licence may be revoked for a breach of these terms.  Revoking a licence stops
   new runs from being authorised; it cannot undo anything you already did.

